# =============================================================================
# AGE Design System — Git attributes for auto-generated files
# =============================================================================
#
# Why: parallel agent worktrees each rebuild and regenerate the tracked files
# below independently per branch.
# Without `merge=ours`, every PR merge would produce conflict markers even
# though the canonical resolution is deterministic — just re-run `yarn build`.
#
# `merge=ours` keeps the current branch's version on merge. It is not a
# built-in driver: `scripts/git/setup-merge-drivers.mjs` (run on `yarn install`)
# registers `merge.ours.driver`; without it git merges these files as text.
# Merge silence is safe because `.husky/pre-push` and the CI "Tokens validation"
# job rebuild and fail when a tracked generated file differs from the build.
#
# `linguist-generated=true` collapses these files in GitHub PR diffs.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Per-component readme.md (stencil build --docs output)
src/components/*/readme.md                                    merge=ours linguist-generated=true
src/hidden/*/readme.md                                        merge=ours linguist-generated=true

# Custom Elements Manifest for Storybook (Stencil docs-custom-elements-manifest output target)
.storybook/custom-elements.json                               merge=ours linguist-generated=true

# Style Dictionary token build outputs (tokens.build wireit target)
tokens/generated/**                                           merge=ours linguist-generated=true

# =============================================================================
# Cross-platform line endings — Windows + Unix contributors coexist on this
# repo. LF for shell scripts, CRLF for PowerShell. Everything else:
# auto-detect, normalize to LF in repo.
# =============================================================================
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
